From 44278dc2d1bc939eac2def97cd50645817a7e14a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 18:59:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09094/11362] Give the mutation-check directory a retention
 policy: 464 MB, 3501 files, no expiry

REQ-OPS-MUTATION-RETENTION-6265. Found while answering "how do we clean things
up?" -- the single biggest thing to clean up was a guard's own debris.

`ops/.test_suite_mutation_runs/` held 3,501 files and 464 MB. 3,441 were
`.writes.log` from runs that finished weeks ago. `prune_stale_markers` retires
MARKERS, which is the interlock's correctness property; nothing ever removed the
two debug files each run leaves behind, so the directory grew without limit. It is
gitignored, so none of it reached history -- this was the operator's disk only.

Deleting once would just let it refill, so this adds `prune_old_debris(days=7)`
and rides it on `--gate`, which runs on every commit. The directory now
self-limits. First run pruned 1,510 files and 174 MB; the remaining 285 MB is
inside the window and ages out on its own.

WHAT IT WILL NOT TOUCH. A `.pending.json` marker, at any age. That is the only
file `--gate` consults, and age is not evidence a rewrite was resolved -- only the
tree is, which is `prune_stale_markers`'s job. An old unresolved rewrite is more
serious than a recent one, not less. A `.snapshot.json` is a baseline only a
matching `--check` reads, and a `--check` a week after its `--snapshot` is
meaningless anyway. A `.writes.log` is read by no code path at all.

FAILS OPEN, which is the opposite of its neighbour and deliberate.
`prune_stale_markers` fails CLOSED because a marker it cannot read might hide real
damage. This one only removes debris, so an undeletable file costs disk and
nothing else. A cleanup routine must never fail the gate it rides on.

Three tests, and the load-bearing one is the marker-survival test -- the whole
risk of putting a deleter next to an interlock is that it deletes the interlock.
Proven to bite by mutation: widening the glob from `*.snapshot.json` to `*.json`
turns that test red. Without that check, the gate could be silenced by waiting.

